          "body": "Steve Tandy will name his Wales squad for the second instalment of the Nations Championship in the coming days, and Wales Online's Steffan Thomas argues Taine Basham has made an undeniable case for inclusion. The 26-year-old, whose last of 17 caps came against England in 2024, has excelled at No 8 for Cardiff since his summer 2025 move from the Dragons, and his discipline has improved markedly. Even in last Saturday's comfortable defeat by Leinster, he stood out against a side packed with British & Irish Lions."
